{"id": "EUVD-2026-103571", "enisaUuid": "4cc8b0a2-dbc2-3d24-9391-0f799c04bde6", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nllc: reserve device headroom for allocated frames\n\nllc_alloc_frame() reserves link-layer headroom using the device type.\nThis is insufficient for stacked Ethernet devices such as VLAN devices,\nwhere vlan_dev_hard_header() pushes a VLAN header before the lower\ndevice's Ethernet header. An LLC response on such a device can\ntherefore underflow skb headroom in eth_header().\n\nUse LL_RESERVED_SPACE() to account for the device's actual required\nheadroom while preserving the existing LLC device-type check.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:17:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:21:07", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/018020f5a48cc86fdd6dc2d380f6c70443ae7639", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3a3f57c4061d9e9cc3bc04205d36ce41ae3406c1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7c38524b2b2456bd33cb360420da6cbf9cad1b33", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1937222c2511ac91377d39f28106c34734f5f8c6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/16ceac2daa89dd16917bc488ab05b9dd6961a603", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e06f8b6e27cc616d3c587e9784c4a033eb310a16", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3361c93e417384ebf28003e0fb6d5304653d3b05", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/72b5b9a28b996e09b8b5b944370c79851bb68f52"], "aliases": ["GHSA-cxpq-4fh3-6276", "CVE-2026-98526"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0c2c21b8-a5b8-3aad-a764-58e6643bf0b6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bf9ae5386bca8836c16e69ab8fdbe46767d7452a <72b5b9a28b996e09b8b5b944370c79851bb68f52"}, {"id": "109be0bb-c318-32d9-a1bc-3c2a50402a3b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bf9ae5386bca8836c16e69ab8fdbe46767d7452a <e06f8b6e27cc616d3c587e9784c4a033eb310a16"}, {"id": "24bc1f3e-254c-39dd-8aa1-a7d377434097", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "2be166d1-837e-3ace-a2ab-9d438130fcc3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bf9ae5386bca8836c16e69ab8fdbe46767d7452a <018020f5a48cc86fdd6dc2d380f6c70443ae7639"}, {"id": "30c9aab1-744d-33e7-998e-1d27582c98a0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "4c3ae210-ee35-39ee-8740-470e6f114252", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "4dbe01f5-20dd-35b0-89a4-c665414629c2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "4ebbbfa9-543b-3a59-a8af-04526dbd9165", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.34"}, {"id": "50192014-1408-32f1-ad46-5e837f320325", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "72dd64bd-93bd-3597-afe2-61bc4dd1e9c8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bf9ae5386bca8836c16e69ab8fdbe46767d7452a <1937222c2511ac91377d39f28106c34734f5f8c6"}, {"id": "7bec853d-3bee-3256-8624-6068f80e1f63", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "85133abc-da6c-3b8a-acdf-1700b5cafa1f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bf9ae5386bca8836c16e69ab8fdbe46767d7452a <16ceac2daa89dd16917bc488ab05b9dd6961a603"}, {"id": "89ab1bb5-4d91-3f6e-981b-267d112bbd89", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bf9ae5386bca8836c16e69ab8fdbe46767d7452a <7c38524b2b2456bd33cb360420da6cbf9cad1b33"}, {"id": "8b723441-ca5b-3b96-92ac-28dc42a62db8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bf9ae5386bca8836c16e69ab8fdbe46767d7452a <3361c93e417384ebf28003e0fb6d5304653d3b05"}, {"id": "8bccec3